# Netlify redirects — awkale.me
#
# Like _headers, this MUST end up in the publish directory (build/client) to take
# effect. Vite copies public/* to the output root, which is why it lives here and
# not at the repo root, where it would be silently ignored.
#
# Thirteen rules, and thirteen is the whole ledger — ADR-0001 as corrected by
# AWK-21. Real 301s are the reason this site is on Netlify at all: ADR-0002 rejected
# GitHub Pages primarily because it cannot issue one, and its closest approximation
# (a stub page carrying <meta http-equiv="refresh">) returns 200 and, for the nine
# cross-origin gist targets, flashes before navigating.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER ADD A CATCH-ALL. This is AWK-17's single most valuable finding, verified
# live: with no catch-all, an unknown path returns a real 404. Add one — a
# /* fallback to /index.html, as an SPA needs — and every unknown path silently
# serves an empty hydration shell instead, across the whole archive. It is also
# what keeps ADR-0001's reserved paths (/music, /2-or-3-things) honestly 404ing
# rather than shipping a blank page.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Sources are written SLASH-FREE, and the live URLs they catch all have trailing
# slashes — the old site was Jekyll with `permalink: pretty`. Netlify normalizes
# trailing slashes when matching, so one rule catches both forms. That assumption
# is not taken on trust: scripts/curl-sweep.sh tests every source in both forms.
#
# All rules are EXACT paths, not splats, so order does not affect matching. The two
# /portfolios/ entries are listed individually rather than as /portfolios/* on
# purpose: a splat would also swallow paths that never existed, and those should
# 404 like anything else.

# --- portfolio ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# All three land on the /projects/ index, NOT on case studies. AWK-21 corrected
# ADR-0001 here: both /portfolios/ entries are Cision items that ship index-only,
# so the case-study pages the original ledger pointed at will never exist. A
# redirect to a case study that was never written is a 404 with extra steps.

/portfolio                       /projects/                                                  301
/portfolios/c3_sidebar           /projects/                                                  301
/portfolios/c3_wizard            /projects/                                                  301

